WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.060
Yakitate!! 9!

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.980
The bread of the first opponent,
Tsubodzuka from CMAP, was...

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.110
Super Toro Aburi.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:12.740
The judge who tasted it couldn’t help
but evolve because of its deliciousness.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.780
Super Kuroyanagi!!

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.370
Kazuma, in reply to the challenge,

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.620
made his Ooma <i>Japan</i>,

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.290
sea urchin chawanmushi-bread made with
Ooma’s specialty eggs and sea urchin.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.750
The winner is Pantasia!

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.590
And I’ll know that immediately after eating this!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.640
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.010
I’ve suddenly grown hair!

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.020
No!

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:41.770
I’ve suddenly been stabbed by hairs!

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.980
Could it be that...?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.480
H-Hair needles?!

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.610
So delicious that it makes your hair fly out, huh?

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.440
I raise the white flag.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.940
Yay.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.620
And then, one clear morning...

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.380
Now, when I think about it, that was where it all began.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.310
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.350
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.480
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.910
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:36.110
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:39.880
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.920
Kuroyanagi in danger!!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.050
The lost reactions!

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:24.140
And now, we’ll have St. Pierre,
who lost in the previous round,

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.010
decide where the second round shall take place.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.070
Say, Azuma...

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.650
This round’s opponent... is...?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.610
It’s been a while.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.150
To think that we’d meet again...

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.650
It’s Ryuu-san!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.780
Wh-Why is Ryuu-san here...?

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.660
That’s simple.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:46.280
I wanted to have an all-out battle with
you guys, now that you’re #1 in the world.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.580
What’s he doing all of a sudden?!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.620
Let’s have a serious match.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.620
Ryuuke Shinken Succession of Kicks!
Prepare yourself!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.670
What’s with this?!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:55.920
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.630
This is a cooking battle, not a kung-fu battle!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.390
Cooking?

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.180
Is that so?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.800
Of course!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.550
Now shut up, will you!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.180
Well, as long as I get paid, I don’t
really care what the rules might be.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.190
Doesn’t he know anything?

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:13.190
Moreover... Can this man make bread?

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:14.400
Well, then.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.110
Would the St. Pierre team pick the next match venue.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.190
All right.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.520
We’ll go with panel #2.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:23.700
Ookuchi?

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.410
Why’s it written in red?

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.240
That is...?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.120
Ookuchi is in the Kagoshima prefecture of Kyuushu.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.500
It refers to the city of Ookuchi in
the Isa region of Kagoshima prefecture.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.380
M-May I ask something, Kuro-yan?

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.710
You’re trying to butt in while I’m talking again?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.300
No, I have a question.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.720
Why is Ookuchi written in red?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.620
That’s because...

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.010
Kumamoto prefecture

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:46.720
Chinese                              Dumplings

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.140
Ch-Chinese dumplings?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.430
That’s right.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.850
For cities in which the item you’re supposed to make is predetermined,

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.390
their name is indicated in red.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.690
So you mean,

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:59.740
we’re supposed to battle it out with Ryuu-san, who’s Chinese, by making Chinese dumplings?

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.240
Isn’t that kinda bad...?

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.160
You’re absolutely right, Kawachi.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.250
M-Manager!

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.540
Where did you come in from?

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.740
In addition to noodles,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:12.250
Ryuu-san is a master cook who has mastered various foods found in Chinese cuisine.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.250
What was that?!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:18.420
The taste of Chinese dumplings is decided by the filling found inside.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.210
In that case...

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:24.970
For this round, we won’t find another
opponent like Ryuu-san anywhere else.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.680
City of Ookuchi

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.470
Boy, what a mess.
City of Ookuchi

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.730
To think that we have Ryuu-san for an opponent...

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:36.730
Yeah, we didn’t learn about anything but yakisoba
and assassination techniques from Ryuu-san...

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.900
We haven’t learned any
assassination techniques!

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.740
And Kanmuri, have you come up with any countermeasures?

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:44.740
Yes, of course.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.200
First, we need high-quality ingredients...

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.950
These are the Isa region’s black hogs,

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.450
considered to be of the highest quality,
even among Kagoshima black hogs.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.630
In the first place, the fillings used
in Chinese dumplings and snacks

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:01.460
usually use ingredients that
are rich in the flavor of pork fat.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.470
So, these hogs are our best option.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.720
Yeah, in Osaka, you actually call
Chinese dumplings “pork dumplings.”

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.650
It would be the most suitable ingredient for this round.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.220
Looks like you also came straight
for the black hogs of Isa, eh?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.980
Huh? Kuro-yan?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.190
What are you doing at a place like this?

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:24.990
Since I’m a judge, it’s required for me
to be more knowledgeable than you guys.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:28.200
So, I’m inspecting the ingredients on my own.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.450
Oh... it looks like being a judge is pretty rough.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.910
I guess there’s more to it than simply
eating bread and doing stupid reactions.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.790
What was that?!

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.750
Sorry for calling your reactions stupid.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.680
Well, that’s how it is.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:50.390
Old Man Kuroyanagi seems really subdued today...

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.520
He’s not going to say anything?

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:55.060
To think that I even thought up a
comeback gag for his comment...

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:58.560
Oh well, let’s leave Kuro-yan aside. Let’s continue, shall we, Kanmuri?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.480
G-Give him an inch and he...

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.490
Oh, whatever.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.570
For some reason, I can’t get worked up today.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.490
Well then, let’s try some immediately.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.120
Oink!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.160
Oink, oink!
Oink!

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.630
That was good.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.840
Wh-What sweetness!

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.290
You wouldn’t think that it’s pork!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.800
It’s so delicious, I think I’ll melt.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.010
For our ingredients this time, it just has to be this.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:31.220
Yeah.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.010
But...

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:38.430
W-With Kuro-yan eating something as delicious
as this, we can expect an extraordinary reaction...

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.740
N-No reaction?!

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.410
That’s shocking!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.120
Wh-What’s wrong, Senpai?!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.120
S-Something’s weird.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.250
Could it be...?

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.120
No, it can’t be.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.130
I’m going to leave now.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.630
O-Okay. Take care.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.100
Guys, I’ll tell you one thing.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:17.230
For a cook, getting self-satisfied can be a fatal flaw.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.770
Don’t forget to continue working diligently.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.770
O-Okay.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:29.950
Don’t you think that his words just now carried
more a feel of a bad omen than that of advice?

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:30.990
A bad omen?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.280
Like, his last words... Or a testament...

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.280
Now that you mention it...

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.000
Don’t be stupid!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.790
You think something like that’s possible with Kuro-yan?!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:40.540
More importantly,

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.170
if we use this meat,

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:45.040
we could probably make delicious Chinese
dumplings without having to work hard at it.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.420
Yeah, that’s true...

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.130
It’s just that this time, the opponent’s also going to be making Chinese dumplings.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.300
I’m sure he’s thought of using black hog meat as well.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.430
To top it off, he’s an expert in Chinese cuisine.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:02.100
If we were to use the same ingredients to make the same thing, there’s no way we’d win.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.900
Not unless we come up with a special strategy.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.520
A special strategy, huh?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.650
This is tough...

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.830
Want me to give you a ride?

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:18.820
Trouble! I’m in trouble!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.570
I-It’s no good.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.360
I can’t taste anything!

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:54.280
I can even eat this god-awful
pigs’ feed like it was nothing.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.370
I guess at that time...

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:06.750
I-I’ve lost my sense of taste...

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:07.830
Senpai.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:09.340
Kuro-yan...

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:14.470
Your sense of taste has gotten messed up,
right, Old Ma... I mean, Mister Kuroyanagi?

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.680
Guys...

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.720
But hey, cheer up!

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.470
I’m sure that if you eat something truly delicious,

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:24.560
your sense of taste and your
crazy reactions will come back.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.240
Something truly delicious, huh?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.450
Right now, anything and everything feels nostalgic.

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:36.700
That’s not true!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:37.820
I’ll make something.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.870
I’ll make you something!

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.620
The most delicious Chinese dumpling.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.830
The Japanese-Style <i>Japan</i>-dumpling.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.870
Japanese-Style <i>Japan</i>-dumpling?

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.630
Are you an idiot, Azuma?!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:49.000
What do you mean by Japanese-style?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.170
This time, we’re supposed to make
Chinese dumplings, not Japanese dumplings.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.380
Oh, is that so?

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:58.350
No. As long as it’s a Chinese dumpling
you make by steaming it in a basket,

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:01.220
it doesn’t matter whether the filling is pizza or curry.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.020
In that case, it’s all right!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:06.100
Just you wait, all right, Old Ma...
I mean Mister Kuroyanagi?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:09.980
I’ll be sure to make you the best
Japanese-Style <i>Japan</i>-dumpling!

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.370
I’m beat.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.540
We really walked a lot today.

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.500
My feet are completely swollen.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.250
But thanks to that, in addition to the black hog,

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:32.050
we got the kinzan leek, a specialty of Ookuchi.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:35.630
As for bonito, we went a little
farther to the Makurazaki area

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.880
to get satsumabushi, a
specialty of Kagoshima prefecture.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.760
With this, tomorrow’s match should be a piece of cake.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.310
No, not yet.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:42.970
What was that?!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:47.600
With these ingredients, I’m sure that
we could make quite a delicious dumpling.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.980
However, unless the dough used to
make the dumpling is delicious, it’s no good.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.480
The dough used for the dumpling?

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:55.990
Well, in Chinese dumplings, the
dough has a tendency to get soggy, right?

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:59.780
If it was merely moist like bread,
I think it’d be more delicious.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:03.120
I understand your feelings, Azuma-kun.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:06.250
You use wheat for the dough of both bread and dumplings,

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.460
so I think you should be able to get similar tastes for both of them.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:12.790
However, Chinese dumplings were made to be steamed.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.170
The dough is 100% made from all-purpose flour.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.790
So, the water content is low.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.970
On the other hand, bread dough, which must be baked,

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:23.260
is made with bread flour, which has a higher water content.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.300
So you can’t get the same taste,
no matter what you do.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.640
You see?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.560
Now stop asking for the impossible.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:32.520
But, if we don’t come up with a strategy for that
part, we won’t be able to win against Ryuu-san,

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:37.110
and we won’t be able to make something delicious
enough to satisfy the present Old Man Kuroyanagi.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.490
So, do you have some kind of plan?

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:40.070
Nope.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.570
You don’t?!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.580
In that case, give up, will ya?

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:45.580
There isn’t even half a day left until the match.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:49.000
How about mixing something into the all-purpose flour?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.580
I guess that might be our only option...

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.540
It can’t be helped.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.710
Shall we go looking for ingredients once again?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.510
You want to go again?

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:58.420
I don’t want to...

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.840
Come on, let’s go, Kawachi-san.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:04.720
If you were to rest here, your
screen time would disappear altogether.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.850
What do you mean, my screen time will disappear?!

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:07.930
Come on, stand up quickly.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.270
It’s impossible, because in addition
to my legs, my hips are tired, too.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.650
Hips?

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:13.220
That’s it!

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:15.480
What happened?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.480
The hips!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.190
We just need to make the dough firmer.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:18.780
The hips?

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:21.320
By “koshi,” you mean the firmness of the dough?

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.530
Yep.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:27.030
But, the dough in Chinese dumplings is already
hard and low in moisture, so how would you...?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.000
It’s all right, Kanmuri.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.620
With a firm <i>Japan</i>-dumpling,
Old Man Kuroyanagi is sure to revive!

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:42.680
Well then, we’ll now start the
second round of Yakitate!! 9!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.590
Both teams, start your work.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.390
In the end, this match has begun
without my sense of taste having returned.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.310
Should there be no miracle to
return my taste to me here...

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.390
I must prepare myself to retire from being a judge.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.320
I wonder what the matter is...

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.990
Kuroyanagi-san seems to be different from usual.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:05.650
I wouldn’t know.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:06.910
It appears to be a slump!

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.790
K-Kawachi-san!

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.210
Isn’t it a bit early for you to be here?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.130
My role is complete with my
having helped them look for ingredients.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.710
There’s no need for a secret weapon
like myself to come out anymore.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.630
Looks like there really is no use for him.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.380
None at all.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:26.600
Either way, what do you mean by a slump?

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.640
It seems that...

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.890
For some reason, since yesterday,

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.890
Kuro-yan’s been unable to taste
anything, no matter what he eats.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:34.900
<i>That</i> Kuroyanagi-san has...?

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:38.820
Because his sense of taste is so much more developed,

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:42.190
it is more delicate than that of a normal person.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:47.900
There’s the possibility that the slightest sickness
can lead to him losing all sense of taste.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.110
Then, today’s reactions might...

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.160
Yeah.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.120
There may not be one.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.370
That is...!

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.880
Wh-What is that?!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:07.800
A technique handed down since ancient times

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:11.510
in the main family of the
Ryuuke Shinken Assassination group.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.890
A legendary technique!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:16.890
Homestyle Chinjao Rosu!

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.230
What was that?!

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:24.440
Looks like you pulled out a big
technique from the very start, huh, Ryuu-san?

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:27.730
This can’t be beat with a little
strategy here and there, Azuma!

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.200
What a nice smell.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.620
This smell...

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:34.540
I see!

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.950
Azuma’s side is doing pretty good, too.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.130
Manager, that is...?

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:40.960
It’s the local sweet potato wine.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:44.800
Kinzan leek, Makurazaki’s
bonito, and sweet potato wine.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:48.460
With all of those, you could create the ultimate filling.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:53.810
But... With just that, I don’t think they
can win against Ryuu-san’s technique.

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.220
That’s not all they’ve got, Manager.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.810
We won’t be finished at this point yet.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.940
There’s a further strategy at this point.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:03.150
What kind of strategy is that?

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.780
You see...

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:06.270
I don’t know!

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.410
There really is no meaning to him being here, huh?

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.030
None at all...

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:14.940
Amazing, Azuma-san!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:16.120
Azuma.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.450
That’s tenobe noodles!

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.040
That manufacturing process makes noodles firm yet moist.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.210
The ultimate technique to bring out the
flavor of the noodles to the maximum...

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:29.210
This would be tenobe dumplings,
and not tenobe noodles!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.260
To think that he knew such a technique!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.300
Just as expected of Azuma!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.060
I’m done.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:38.060
This is my Complete Family
Register of Chinese Dumplings.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.150
It looks like the time has arrived.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:45.560
This time, in addition to myself, a
special judge has been called upon.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:50.570
Looks like he’s arranged for an alternate
judge because of his lost sense of taste.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:54.530
Pantasia General Manager Meister Kirisaki...

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:57.080
M-Meister is here?!

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.000
...his pet.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.170
Coo-san, the peacock.

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:06.960
Wh-What does this mean?!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:10.510
While he may be a peacock, he <i>is</i> Meister’s pet.

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:15.100
He can pass along a better judgment than the average judge that you’d find just anywhere.

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:17.800
But even then, having a bird as the judge is just...

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.720
Well then...

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.110
Oh. He displayed his feathers fully.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.480
Wh-What do you mean?

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:34.070
He expresses deliciousness by
opening his feathers at a certain angle.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:35.450
Fully displaying his feathers means full points.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.990
Wh-What was that?!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.880
What about Kuro-yan...?

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.790
G-Guess it was no good...

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:46.210
To think that my sense of taste still hasn’t returned...

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.800
I am left with no choice but to
make a decision right here, right now.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:54.800
I, Kuroyanagi Ryou, as of today...

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:59.270
resign from my position of Judge of
Yakitate!! 9, and that of taste judge!

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.520
What was that?!

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:01.720
Kuroyanagi-san!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:06.270
Wait, Old Ma... I mean Mister Kuroyanagi!

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.770
Quit only after having tasted mine.

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:10.270
Azuma...

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.610
This is my Chinese dumpling,

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.780
the Japanese-Style, <i>Japan</i>-dumpling
made using the tenobe technique!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.120
You can always quit after having tasted mine.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.290
Very well.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.490
You’re right.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.250
But...

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.000
Senpai...

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:30.170
Kuro-yan...

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:33.300
Don’t make such a scary face.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.050
You just have to believe in me and eat it.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:54.740
Oh, no!

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:56.530
This is no time to be having a reaction!

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.240
Shut up, Kawachi.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.660
A topknot?

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:06.200
Did Kuro-yan get himself a topknot because the taste is Japanese-style?

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.540
No!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:12.590
With that kind of wimpy reaction, you can’t
say that Kuroyanagi had a complete recovery!

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.510
Look carefully!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:18.670
Pafu Pafu. Pafu Pafu.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:22.270
Wh-What the... What’s Kuro-yan doing?

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:23.480
Did he break?

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.190
Don’t you get it, Kawachi?

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.730
He’s doing a Pafu Pafu.
Note: Pafu Pafu (<b>ぱふぱふ) is onomatopoeia for puffiness or fluffiness.</b>

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:28.270
Pafu Pafu?

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.770
Pafu Pafu. Pafu Pafu.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.020
Wafu Pafu.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.270
Wafu Wafu.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.650
Wafuu Wafuu.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:34.990
Note: Wafuu (<b>和風) means “Japanese-style.”</b>

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.280
Japanese-Style <i>Japan</i>-dumpling!

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.490
All right!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.830
We finally have the revival of the reactions!

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.780
But, it’s amazing that he can
do something gross like that.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:49.950
Even I would have preferred to do it with a woman!

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:52.300
Hi-His hands are stretching!

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:55.210
I’m no longer the Tenobe-dumpling.
I’m now the tenobi man!

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:57.170
So, why’s he wearing a straw hat?

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.470
Tenobi Man
So, why’s he wearing a straw hat?

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.800
The tenobi... No, tenobe dumplings are delicious!
Tenobi Man

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:04.980
Azuma!

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:07.520
This satsumabushi you used in
the Japanese-style soup stock...

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:11.230
The Kagoshima prefecture holds pride in the
fact that they produce the best bonito in Japan.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:16.400
And from those bonito, the
satsumabushi is considered to be the best.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:20.650
It’s no exaggeration to call the stock
you make from that the “ultimate taste.”

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.080
And... This sweet potato wine!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:26.000
Ookuchi is supposed to be the place
from which sweet potato wine originated.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.920
The weakness of the dumpling is that it
gets hard when steamed for a long time.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.210
You’ve overcome that by using Ookuchi’s liquor,

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:35.540
also creating a soft flavor that
brings out the flavor of the meat perfectly.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.090
And, and...

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.720
The biggest point to note is... This dough!

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:41.970
It has much more bread flour
than a regular Chinese dumpling.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.930
By making it more like bread, you’ve made it softer!

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.390
Th-That’s right...

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.440
And, on top of that...

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:52.480
By this tenobi... I mean tenobe technique,
you’ve gotten it to be firm, yet moist.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.110
The dough really matches the Japanese-style taste.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:21:00.040
It’s truly delicious!
The Japanese-Style <i>Japan</i>-dumpling!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.530
The winner: Pantasia!

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.030
All right!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.240
Yay!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.460
I-I can’t accept that!

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:12.130
If your sense of taste is back,
then you should rejudge mine.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:13.420
There’s no need for that.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:14.410
Wh-Why not?

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.380
Your Complete Family Register of
Chinese Dumplings were delicious,

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:19.550
as shown by the peacock Coo.

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:20.680
But, however.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:23.420
The filling only has one
specialty of Ookuchi, the black hog.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:32.680
At Yakitate!! 9, you get more points for using
more specialties from the region assigned!

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:38.070
Also, Azuma’s Chinese dumplings were so
delicious that they brought back my sense of taste,

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:41.240
something that yours couldn’t do.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.370
So whatchuu shay ish that... It worksh out thish way...?

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:46.370
However, it’s true that your
Chinese dumplings are the real thing.

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:49.660
Normally, peacocks are flightless birds.

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:52.160
But, Coo is expressing its deliciousness in that manner.

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:57.430
So, if you insist on my eating it once again, then...

00:21:57.430 --> 00:21:58.800
I will be happy to oblige!

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.550
Well, I’m glad we won.

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:04.000
And, he returned to being normal Kuroyanagi-san.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:07.850
I’m glad that Old Man Kuroyanagi
was able to get back to normal.

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:11.020
We’ll be able to see his reactions as usual once again.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:13.060
Oh boy...

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:16.520
Isn’t he even more excited
than he usually is?

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:18.400
This shark fin dumpling is delicious!

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.520
This bear paw dumpling is delicious too!

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:21.800
No!

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:24.250
I want to eat that.

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:27.080
In this manner, I was able
to get back to my normal self.

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:28.080
Wait!

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.290
That’s mine! Give it back to me!
In this manner, I was able
to get back to my normal self.

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:30.120
Give it back! Give it back!

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:31.300
All’s well that ends well!
Give it back! Give it back!

00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:33.380
All’s well that ends well!

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:07.050
CMAP’s gonna get serious.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:08.220
What was that?!

00:24:08.220 --> 00:24:13.010
The Cooking Meal Assemble People are going to...?

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.930
Looks like he just wanted to say that.

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:16.390
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:17.520
Ooo, mango!!

00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:18.940
CMAP’s big counterattack!

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:19.890
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:22.640
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:22.940
Varieties of wheat flour

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:24.420
Wheat flours are broadly divided into three
varieties depending on their protein content.
Varieties of wheat flour

00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:27.030
Protein content

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:27.120
In decreasing order of
protein content, they are called...
Varieties of wheat flour

00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:27.280
High

00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:28.220
Low

00:24:28.220 --> 00:24:28.700
Bread flour

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:28.990
Bread flour, all-purpose flour,
and low-viscosity wheat flour.

00:24:28.990 --> 00:24:29.750
All-purpose flour
Bread flour, all-purpose flour,
and low-viscosity wheat flour.

00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:31.660
Low-viscosity
wheat flour
All-purpose flour

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.540
Oh?!
